To find the CSS code for a light red color with a medium light shade of pink, we can use the RGB or HEX color codes. Here are a few options:

1. RGB:
```css
lightred {
  color: rgb(255, 182, 193);
  background-color: rgb(255, 182, 193);
}
```

2. HEX:
```css
lightred {
  color: #FFB6C1;
  background-color: #FFB6C1;
}
```

These codes will give you a light red color with a medium light shade of pink. You can apply this class to any HTML element to change its color or background color. For example:

```html
<p class="lightred">This is a light red text with a medium light shade of pink background.</p>
```
